{
  "esm": "0.7.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "ERA5",
    "description": "ERA5 regridding model — the coupler half of the era5 loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; bead esm-3nc.1). Exposes ERA5 ECMWF Reanalysis 5th Generation pressure-level fields on the simulation's target grid for coupling into EarthSciML systems.\n\nStructure (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6):\n  1. It declares the pure-I/O loader (components/earthsci_data/era5_loader.esm) as the subsystem `pl` via {\"ref\": \"./era5_loader.esm\"}. Loader fields are referenced as ERA5.pl.<var> (e.g. ERA5.pl.u).\n  2. Reprojection: ERA5's native grid is geographic (longlat/WGS84), so the coordinate transform is the longlat IDENTITY (ESD reprojection/longlat.esm, esd-47z.1) — selected by convention from the loader's grid.crs.projection = 'longlat'; a no-op for an unprojected grid.\n  3. Regridding (per variable, RFC §5.2): the horizontal wind components u, v use B-spline interpolation; all centered scalars (temperature, humidity, geopotential, cloud, ozone, vorticity/divergence, and the vertical-velocity field w) use conservative (area-weighted, mass-conserving) regridding. Declared in the `regrid` block.\n\nTop-level derived quantities computed on the target grid: pressure P (from the 37-entry pressure-level lookup table), and the lat/lon coordinate metrics δxδlon and δyδlat (emitted only for lat/lon coordinate domains).\n\nMeanWind coupling (from EarthSciData.jl@830435a coupling.jl): MeanWind.v_lon ~ ERA5.pl.u, MeanWind.v_lat ~ ERA5.pl.v, MeanWind.v_lev ~ ERA5.pl.w.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/era5.jl:385 (ERA5 constructor, esm-te2e); split into pure loader + regridding model by esm-3nc.1.",
    "tags": [
